Parity reproduced exactly from the web source (cross-platform value parity, not a "corrected" version):
  arrived_at    = <TimeStamp format="absolute" />  → localized medium date + short time, "—" when unparseable
  reason/vin/topic = mono cells, "—" via (parsed_reason || '—') / (parsed_vin ?? '—') / (topic ?? '—')
  redeliveries  = parsed_redeliveries != null ? fmtInt(v) : "—"   (Intl.NumberFormat grouping, locale-aware)
  payload       = formatBytes(raw_payload_size)  [ "—" for <0 · "N B" <1KiB · "X.X KB" <1MiB · "X.X MB" ;
                  the toFixed(1) decimal rendered with a '.' separator, locale-independent, as in JS ]
  replayable    = replayable ? Badge(success,"Yes") : Badge(neutral,"No")
  actions       = secondary/sm Button "Inspect" → onInspect(row)  (parent owns the drawer, web onInspect prop)
  sort          = useSortToggle('arrived_at','desc'): default arrived desc; sortable arrived_at (date) /
                  parsed_reason (localeCompare) / parsed_vin ((x ?? '').localeCompare) / raw_payload_size
                  (numeric); stable (ties preserve order).

States reproduced (every one renders — no hidden surfaces; each has a #if DEBUG preview):
  loading (skeleton + "Loading…") · loading-behind-cache · loaded · empty ("No DLQ entries — the pipeline is
  clean.") · error (TSErrorDisplay + retry) · error-behind-cache (banner + retry + cached table) · stale
  (chip + banner) · offline (chip + banner + cached table).

